to get the full content if needed.\n\nFound function `benchmarks/bench_online_ocsvm.py:print_outlier_ratio`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n41 | def print_outlier_ratio(y):\n42 |     \"\"\"\n43 |     Helper function to show the distinct value count of element in the target.\n44 |     Useful indicator for the datasets used in bench_isolation_forest.py.\n45 |     \"\"\"\n46 |     uniq, cnt = np.unique(y, return_counts=True)\n47 |     print(\"----- Target count values: \")\n48 |     for u, c in zip(uniq, cnt):\n49 |         print(\"------ %s -> %d occurrences\" % (str(u), c))\n50 |     print(\"----- Outlier ratio: %.5f\" % (np.min(cnt) / len(y)))\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_dict_learning.py:_update_dict`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n415 | def _update_dict(\n416 |     dictionary,\n417 |     Y,\n418 |     code,\n419 |     A=None,\n420 |     B=None,\n421 |     verbose=False,\n422 |     random_state=None,\n423 |     positive=False,\n424 | ):\n425 |     \"\"\"Update the dense dictionary factor in place.\n426 | \n427 |     Parameters\n428 |     ----------\n429 |     dictionary : ndarray of shape (n_components, n_features)\n430 |         Value of the dictionary at the previous iteration.\n431 | \n432 |     Y : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n433 |         Data matrix.\n434 | \n435 |     code : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n436 |         Sparse coding of the data against which to optimize the dictionary.\n437 | \n438 |     A : ndarray of shape (n_components, n_components), default=None\n439 |         Together with `B`, sufficient stats of the online model to update the\n440 |         dictionary.\n441 | \n442 |     B : ndarray of shape (n_features, n_components), default=None\n443 |         Together with `A`, sufficient stats of the online model to update the\n444 |         dictionary.\n445 | \n446 |     verbose: bool, default=False\n447 |         Degree of output the