orer : callable\n413 |         The scorer.\n414 | \n415 |     Notes\n416 |     -----\n417 |     When passed a string, this function always returns a copy of the scorer\n418 |     object. Calling `get_scorer` twice for the same scorer results in two\n419 |     separate scorer objects.\n420 | \n421 |     Examples\n422 |     --------\n423 |     >>> import numpy as np\n424 |     >>> from sklearn.dummy import DummyClassifier\n425 |     >>> from sklearn.metrics import get_scorer\n426 |     >>> X = np.reshape([0, 1, -1, -0.5, 2], (-1, 1))\n427 |     >>> y = np.array([0, 1, 1, 0, 1])\n428 |     >>> classifier = DummyClassifier(strategy=\"constant\", constant=0).fit(X, y)\n429 |     >>> accuracy = get_scorer(\"accuracy\")\n430 |     >>> accuracy(classifier, X, y)\n431 |     0.4\n432 |     \"\"\"\n433 |     if isinstance(scoring, str):\n434 |         try:\n435 |             if scoring == \"max_error\":\n436 |                 # TODO (1.8): scoring=\"max_error\" has been deprecated in 1.6,\n437 |                 # remove in 1.8\n438 |                 scorer = max_error_scorer\n439 |             else:\n440 |                 scorer = copy.deepcopy(_SCORERS[scoring])\n441 |         except KeyError:\n442 |             raise ValueError(\n443 |                 \"%r is not a valid scoring value. \"\n444 |                 \"Use sklearn.metrics.get_scorer_names() \"\n445 |                 \"to get valid options.\" % scoring\n446 |             )\n447 |     else:\n448 |         scorer = scoring\n449 |     return scorer\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_mask.py:_get_mask`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n38 | def _get_mask(X, value_to_mask):\n39 |     \"\"\"Compute the boolean mask X == value_to_mask.\n40 | \n41 |     Parameters\n42 |     ----------\n43 |     X : {ndarray, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n44 |         Input data, where ``n_samples`` is the number of samples and\n45 |         ``n_features`` is the number of features.\n46 | \n47 |     value_to_mask : {int, float}\n48 |         The value which is to be masked in X.\n49 | \n50 |     Returns\n51 |     -------\n52 |     X_mask : {ndarray, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n53 |         Missing mask.\n54 |     \"\"\"\n55 |     if not sp.issparse(X):\n56 |         # For all cases apart of a sparse input where we need to reconstruct\n57 |         # a sparse output\n58 |         return _get_dense_mask(X, value_to_mask)\n59 | \n60 |     Xt = _get_dense_mask(X.data, value_to_mask)\n61 | \n62 |     sparse_constructor = sp.csr_matrix if X.format == \"csr\" else sp.csc_matrix\n63 |     Xt_sparse = sparse_constructor(\n64 |         (Xt, X.indices.copy(), X.indptr.copy()), shape=X.shape, dtype=bool\n65 |     )\n66 | \n67 |     return Xt_sparse\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me examine the base estimator implementation since it's central to the issue:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`.\n```\n392 | def __sklearn_tags__(self):\n393 |         return Tags(\n394 |             estimator_type=None,\n395 |             target_tags=TargetTags(required=False),\n396 |             transformer_tags=None,\n397 |             regressor_tags=None,\n398 |             classifier_tags=None,\n399 |         )\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, I can now provide the locations that need modification to implement the requested feature. Here's the final output:\n\n```\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 293-334\nfunction: get_tags\ndescription: Main function nee