ven an estimator and some data.\n198 | \n199 |         Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <confusion_matrix>`.\n200 | \n201 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0\n202 | \n203 |         Parameters\n204 |         ----------\n205 |         estimator : estimator instance\n206 |             Fitted classifier or a fitted :class:`~sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`\n207 |             in which the last estimator is a classifier.\n208 | \n209 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n210 |             Input values.\n211 | \n212 |         y : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n213 |             Target values.\n214 | \n215 |         labels : array-like of shape (n_classes,), default=None\n216 |             List of labels to index the confusion matrix. This may be used to\n217 |             reorder or select a subset of labels. If `None` is given, those\n218 |             that appear at least once in `y_true` or `y_pred` are used in\n219 |             sorted order.\n220 | \n221 |         sample_weight : array-like of shape (n_samples,), default=None\n222 |             Sample weights.\n223 | \n224 |         normalize : {'true', 'pred', 'all'}, default=None\n225 |             Either to normalize the counts display in the matrix:\n226 | \n227 |             - if `'true'`, the confusion matrix is normalized over the true\n228 |               conditions (e.g. rows);\n229 |             - if `'pred'`, the confusion matrix is normalized over the\n230 |               predicted conditions (e.g. columns);\n231 |             - if `'all'`, the confusion matrix is normalized by the total\n232 |               number of samples;\n233 |             - if `None` (default), the confusion matrix will not be normalized.\n234 | \n235 |         display_labels : array-like of shape (n_classes,), default=None\n236 |             Target names used for plotting. By default, `labels` will be used\n237 |             if it is defined, otherwise the unique labels of `y_true` and\n238 |             `y_pred` will be used.\n239 | \n240 |         include_values : bool, default=True\n241 |             Includes values in confusion matrix.\n242 | \n243 |         xticks_rotation : {'vertical', 'horizontal'} or float, \\\n244 |                 default='horizontal'\n245 |             Rotation of xtick labels.\n246 | \n247 |         values_format : str, default=None\n248 |             Format specification for values in confusion matrix. If `None`, the\n249 |             format specification is 'd' or '.2g' whichever is shorter.\n250 | \n251 |         cmap : str or matplotlib Colormap, default='viridis'\n252 |             Colormap recognized by matplotlib.\n253 | \n254 |         ax : matplotlib Axes, default=None\n255 |             Axes object to plot on. If `None`, a new figure and axes is\n256 |             created.\n257 | \n258 |         colorbar : bool, default=True\n259 |             Whether or not to add a colorbar to the plot.\n260 | \n261 |         Returns\n262 |         -------\n263 |         display : :class:`~sklearn.metrics.ConfusionMatrixDisplay`\n264 | \n265 |         See Also\n266 |         --------\n267 |         ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_predictions : Plot the confusion matrix\n268 |             given the true and predicted labels.\n269 | \n270 |         Examples\n271 |         --------\n272 |         >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n273 |         >>> from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n274 |         >>> from sklearn.metrics import ConfusionMatrixDisplay\n275 |         >>> from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n276 |         >>> from sklearn.svm import SVC\n277 |         >>> X, y = make_classification(random_state=0)\n278 |         >>> X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n279 |         ...         X, y, random_state=0)\n280 |         >>> clf = SVC(random_state=0)\n281 |         >>> clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n282 |         SVC(random_state=0)\n283 |         >>> ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_estimator(\n284 |         ...     clf, X_test, y_test)\n285 |         <...>\n286 |         >>> plt.show()\n287 |         \"\"\"\n288 |         method_name = f\"{cls.__name__}.from_estimator\"\n289 |         check_matplotlib_support(method_name)\n290 |         if not is_classifier(estimator):\n291 |             raise ValueError(f\"{method_name} only supports classifiers\")\n292 |         y_pred = estimator.predict(X)\n293 | \n294 |         return cls.from_predictions(\n295 |             y,\n296 |             y_pred,\n297 |             sample_weight=sample_weight,\n298 |             labels=labels,\n299 |             normalize=normalize,\n300 |             display_labels=display_labels,\n301 |             include_values=include_values,\n302 |             cmap=cmap,\n303 |             ax=ax,\n304 |             xticks_rotation=xticks_rotation,\n305 |             values_format=values_format,\n306 |             colorbar=colorbar,\n307 |         )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay.from_predictions`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n191 | def from_predictions(\n192 |         cls,\n193 |         y_true,\n194 |         y_pred,\n195 |         *,\n196 |         sample_weight=None,\n197 |         pos_label=None,\n198 |         name=None,\n199 |         ax=None,\n200 |         **kwargs,\n201 |     ):\n202 |         \"\"\"Plot DET curve given the true and\n203 |         predicted labels.\n204 | \n205 |         Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <visualizations>`.\n206 | \n207 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0\n208 | \n209 |         Parameters\n210 |         ----------\n211 |         y_true : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n212 |             True labels.\n213 | \n214 |         y_pred : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n215 |             Target scores, can either be probability estimates of the positive\n216 |             class, confidence values, or non-thresholded measure of decisions\n217 |             (as returned by