n\nFound function `sympy/polys/polyclasses.py:DUP_Flint.abs`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1922 | def abs(f):\n1923 |         \"\"\"Make all coefficients in ``f`` positive. \"\"\"\n1924 |         return f.to_DMP_Python().abs().to_DUP_Flint()\n```\n\nFound function `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:Abs.fdiff`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n512 | def fdiff(self, argindex=1):\n513 |         \"\"\"\n514 |         Get the first derivative of the argument to Abs().\n515 | \n516 |         \"\"\"\n517 |         if argindex == 1:\n518 |             return sign(self.args[0])\n519 |         else:\n520 |             raise ArgumentIndexError(self, argindex)\n```\n\nFound function `sympy/matrices/matrixbase.py:MatrixBase.refine`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2355 | def refine(self, assumptions=True):\n2356 |         \"\"\"Apply refine to each element of the matrix.\n2357 | \n2358 |         Examples\n2359 |         ========\n2360 | \n2361 |         >>> from sympy import Symbol, Matrix, Abs, sqrt, Q\n2362 |         >>> x = Symbol('x')\n2363 |         >>> Matrix([[Abs(x)**2, sqrt(x**2)],[sqrt(x**2), Abs(x)**2]])\n2364 |         Matrix([\n2365 |         [ Abs(x)**2, sqrt(x**2)],\n2366 |         [sqrt(x**2),  Abs(x)**2]])\n2367 |         >>> _.refine(Q.real(x))\n2368 |         Matrix([\n2369 |         [  x**2, Abs(x)],\n2370 |         [Abs(x),   x**2]])\n2371 | \n2372 |         \"\"\"\n2373 |         return self.applyfunc(lambda x: refine(x, assumptions))\n```\n\nFound function `sympy/matrices/common.py:MatrixOperations.refine`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2331 | def refine(self, assumptions=True):\n2332 |         \"\"\"Apply refine to each element of the matrix.\n2333 | \n2334 |         Examples\n2335 |         ========\n2336 | \n2337 |         >>> from sympy import Symbol, Matrix, Abs, sqrt, Q\n2338 |         >>> x = Symbol('x')\n23