keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 4 | from .validation import check_random_state\n 5 | \n 6 | \n 7 | def _init_arpack_v0(size, random_state):\n 8 |     \"\"\"Initialize the starting vector for iteration in ARPACK functions.\n 9 | \n10 |     Initialize a ndarray with values sampled from the uniform distribution on\n11 |     [-1, 1]. This initialization model has been chosen to be consistent with\n12 |     the ARPACK one as another initialization can lead to convergence issues.\n13 | \n14 |     Parameters\n15 |     ----------\n16 |     size : int\n17 |         The size of the eigenvalue vector to be initialized.\n18 | \n19 |     random_state : int, RandomState instance or None, default=None\n20 |         The seed of the pseudo random number generator used to generate a\n21 |         uniform distribution. If int, random_state is the seed used by the\n22 |         random number generator; If RandomState instance, random_state is the\n23 |         random number generator; If None, the random number generator is the\n24 |         RandomState instance used by `np.random`.\n25 | \n26 |     Returns\n27 |     -------\n28 |     v0 : ndarray of shape (size,)\n29 |         The initialized vector.\n30 |     \"\"\"\n31 |     random_state = check_random_state(random_state)\n32 |     v0 = random_state.uniform(-1, 1, size)\n33 |     return v0\n34 | \n```\n\nFound code snippet in file `examples/inspection/plot_permutation_importance_multicollinear.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"\n  2 | =================================================================\n  3 | Permutation Importance with Multicollinear or Correlated Features\n  4 | =================================================================\n  5 | \n  6 | In this example, we compute the\n  7 | :func:`~sklearn.inspection.permutation_importance` of the features to a trained\n  8 | :class:`~sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier` using the\n  9 | :ref:`breast_cancer_dataset`. The model can easily get about 97% accuracy on a\n 10 | test dataset. Because this dataset contains multicollinear features, the\n 11 | permutation importance shows that none of the features are important, in\n 12 | contradiction with the high test accuracy.\n 13 | \n 14 | We demo a possible approach to handling multicollinearity, which consists of\n 15 | hierarchical clustering on the features' Spearman rank-order correlations,\n 16 | picking a threshold, and keeping a single feature from each cluster.\n 17 | \n 18 | .. note::\n 19 |     See also\n 20 |     :ref:`sphx_glr_auto_examples_inspection_plot_permutation_importance.py`\n 21 | \n 22 | \"\"\"\n 23 | \n 24 | # Authors: The scikit-learn developers\n 25 | # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause\n 26 | \n 27 | # %%\n 28 | # Random Forest Feature Importance on Breast Cancer Data\n 29 | # ------------------------------------------------------\n 30 | #\n 31 | # First, we define a function to ease the plotting:\n 32 | import matplotlib\n 33 | \n 34 | from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\n 35 | from sklearn.utils.fixes import parse_version\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/validation.py:_check_pos_label_consistency`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2529 | def _check_pos_label_consistency(pos_label, y_true):\n2530 |     \"\"\"Check if `pos_label` need to be specified or not.\n2531 | \n2532 |     In binary classification, we fix `pos_label=1` if the labels are in the set\n2533 |     {-1, 1} or {0, 1}. Otherwise, we raise an error asking to specify the\n2534 |     `pos_label` parameters.\n2535 | \n2536 |     Parameters\n2537 |     ----------\n2538 |     pos_label : int, float, bool, str or None\n2539 |         The positive label.\n2540 |     y_true : ndarray of shape (n_samples,)\n2541 |         The target vector.\n2542 | \n2543 |     Returns\n2544 |     -------\n2545 |     pos_label : int, float, bool or str\n2546 |         If `pos_label` can be inferred, it will be returned.\n2547 | \n2548 |     Raises\n2549 |     ------\n2550 |     ValueError\n2551 |         In the case that `y_true` does not have label in {-1, 1} or {0, 1},\n2552 |         it will raise a `ValueError`.\n2553 |     \"\"\"\n2554 |     # ensure binary classification if pos_label is not specified\n2555 |     # classes.dtype.kind in ('O', 'U', 'S') is required to avoid\n2556 |     # triggering a FutureWarning by calling np.array_equal(a, b)\n2557 |     # when elements in the two arrays are not comparable.\n2558 |     if pos_label is None:\n2559 |         # Compute classes only if pos_label is not specified:\n2560 |         classes = np.unique(y_true)\n2561 |         if classes.dtype.kind in \"OUS\" or not (\n2562 |             np.array_equal(classes, [0, 1])\n2563 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1, 1])\n2564 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [0])\n2565 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1])\n2566 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [1])\n2567 |         ):\n2568 |             classes_repr = \", \".join([repr(c) for c in classes.tolist()])\n2569 |             raise ValueError(\n2570 |                 f\"y_true takes value in {{{classes_repr}}} and pos_label is not \"\n2571 |                 \"specified: either make y_true take value in {0, 1} or \"\n2572 |                 \"{-1, 1} or pass pos_label explicitly.\"\n2573 |             )\n2574 |         pos_label = 1\n2575 | \n2576 |     return pos_label\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/cluster/_optics.py:_compute_core_distances_`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n408 | def _compute_core_distances_(X, neighbors, min_samples, working_memory):\n409 |     \"\"\"Compute the k-th nearest neighbor of each sample.\n410 | \n411 |     Equivalent to neighbors.kneighbors(X, self.min_samples)[0][:, -1]\n412 |     but with more memory efficiency.\n413 | \n414 |     Parameters\n415 |     ----------\n416 |     X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n417 |         The data.\n418 