he bootstrap procedure is performed.\n324 |     **kwds\n325 |         Options to pass to matplotlib plotting method.\n326 | \n327 |     Returns\n328 |     -------\n329 |     matplotlib.figure.Figure\n330 |         Matplotlib figure.\n331 | \n332 |     See Also\n333 |     --------\n334 |     DataFrame.plot : Basic plotting for DataFrame objects.\n335 |     Series.plot : Basic plotting for Series objects.\n336 | \n337 |     Examples\n338 |     --------\n339 |     This example draws a basic bootstrap plot for a Series.\n340 | \n341 |     .. plot::\n342 |         :context: close-figs\n343 | \n344 |         >>> s = pd.Series(np.random.uniform(size=100))\n345 |         >>> pd.plotting.bootstrap_plot(s)\n346 |         <Figure size 640x480 with 6 Axes>\n347 |     \"\"\"\n348 |     plot_backend = _get_plot_backend(\"matplotlib\")\n349 |     return plot_backend.bootstrap_plot(\n350 |         series=series, fig=fig, size=size, samples=samples, **kwds\n351 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/hist.py:hist_series`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n356 | def hist_series(\n357 |     self,\n358 |     by=None,\n359 |     ax=None,\n360 |     grid=True,\n361 |     xlabelsize=None,\n362 |     xrot=None,\n363 |     ylabelsize=None,\n364 |     yrot=None,\n365 |     figsize=None,\n366 |     bins=10,\n367 |     legend: bool = False,\n368 |     **kwds,\n369 | ):\n370 |     import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n371 | \n372 |     if legend and \"label\" in kwds:\n373 |         raise ValueError(\"Cannot use both legend and label\")\n374 | \n375 |     if by is None:\n376 |         if kwds.get(\"layout\", None) is not None:\n377 |             raise ValueError(\"The 'layout' keyword is not supported when 'by' is None\")\n378 |         # hack until the plotting interface is a bit more unified\n379 |         fig = kwds.pop(\n380 |             \"figure\", plt.gcf() if plt.get_fignums() else plt.figure(figsize=figsize)\n381 |         )\n382 |       