sing keyword search (bm25).\n```\n968 | def _get_axes_layout(self) -> tuple[int, int]:\n969 |         axes = self._get_subplots()\n970 |         x_set = set()\n971 |         y_set = set()\n972 |         for ax in axes:\n973 |             # check axes coordinates to estimate layout\n974 |             points = ax.get_position().get_points()\n975 |             x_set.add(points[0][0])\n976 |             y_set.add(points[0][1])\n977 |         return (len(y_set), len(x_set))\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/tools.py:handle_shared_axes`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n381 | def handle_shared_axes(\n382 |     axarr: Iterable[Axes],\n383 |     nplots: int,\n384 |     naxes: int,\n385 |     nrows: int,\n386 |     ncols: int,\n387 |     sharex: bool,\n388 |     sharey: bool,\n389 | ):\n390 |     if nplots > 1:\n391 |         row_num = lambda x: x.get_subplotspec().rowspan.start\n392 |         col_num = lambda x: x.get_subplotspec().colspan.start\n393 | \n394 |         if compat.mpl_ge_3_4_0():\n395 |             is_first_col = lambda x: x.get_subplotspec().is_first_col()\n396 |         else:\n397 |             is_first_col = lambda x: x.is_first_col()\n398 | \n399 |         if nrows > 1:\n400 |             try:\n401 |                 # first find out the ax layout,\n402 |                 # so that we can correctly handle 'gaps\"\n403 |                 layout = np.zeros((nrows + 1, ncols + 1), dtype=np.bool_)\n404 |                 for ax in axarr:\n405 |                     layout[row_num(ax), col_num(ax)] = ax.get_visible()\n406 | \n407 |                 for ax in axarr:\n408 |                     # only the last row of subplots should get x labels -> all\n409 |                     # other off layout handles the case that the subplot is\n410 |                     # the last in the column, because below is no subplot/gap.\n411 |                     if not layout[row_num(ax) + 1, col_num(ax)]:\n412 |                        